{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfukWwr9wmb25x5sF6hKG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not really, at least not as a built-in deploy option. When you run `wrangler deploy`, Cloudflare updates the Worker script, and existing Durable Object instances get moved to the new code the next time they're activated, while any instance that's already running keeps its current code until it's evicted or restarts. You can't set a per-class grace period for this. The practical approaches are to keep your DO code backward compatible across deploys, or to use a version-tag pattern where the Worker routes requests to a specific class version. If you need a hard guarantee that old instances finish on old code, you'd have to handle that yourself, for example by draining or versioning the objects in your application logic."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3040,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3040},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6af5d776-9cc3-4b24-9fe1-2ba789d60057","uuid":"a86e3898-0910-44f8-a0e6-fa1bdcd11e74","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:37:00.886Z","request_id":"req_011CfukWweknRH4SHrdvgYj6"}
